# This directory is the one that includes `llvm/*`, and one analyzer check cannot
# be told that those headers are not ours.
#
# `clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound` fires on LLVM's own code reachable from
# here -- `User.h`'s hung-off operands (`*(reinterpret_cast<Use **>(this) - 1)`),
# which is a deliberate negative index, and the operand accessor in
# `InstrTypes.h` that reaches it through an `assert`. The report is classified as
# user code however `--header-filter` or `--exclude-header-filter` is set, because
# the path begins in this translation unit, so there is no way to scope the check
# to our own lines while an LLVM header is in the file. It is turned off here and
# nowhere else: every module that does not cross the LLVM boundary still runs it.
#
# `InheritParentConfig` is what keeps this a subtraction rather than a
# replacement -- without it the `Checks` list below would drop every check the
# root `.clang-tidy` enables.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >-
  -clang-analyzer-security.ArrayBound
